{
  "_doc": [
    "CRAFTING \u2014 the single source of truth, read by BOTH the client (fetched at",
    "boot, js/game3d.js) and the server (required by server/tx.js).",
    "",
    "It exists because the costs used to be stated TWICE in the client, once in",
    "canCraft() as a >= check and again in doCraft() as a subtraction. Nothing kept",
    "the two in step, and adding a third statement on the server would have made a",
    "silent, exploitable disagreement inevitable \u2014 a recipe the client thinks costs",
    "3 and the server thinks costs 4 is a rejection the player cannot understand.",
    "",
    "FIELDS",
    "  cost      items consumed on success.",
    "  requires  items that must be HELD but are NOT consumed (see 'wall').",
    "  gain      items produced.",
    "  placeable a placeable granted to the pack; placeCount defaults to 1. The",
    "            inventory key equals the placeable type for every entry in",
    "            PLACEABLES, which is why one name does for both.",
    "  tool      sets player.has<Tool> true.",
    "  tier      sets a tool tier, e.g. {\"sword\": 2}.",
    "  armor     equips an armor piece of that material rank (equipArmorPiece).",
    "  build     opens build mode for that item instead of yielding anything.",
    "  near      proximity gate. 'workbench' | 'forge' \u2014 satisfied by ANY listed",
    "            one unless nearAll is true. 'forge' is also satisfied by standing",
    "            at the town blacksmith, matching the client's long-standing rule.",
    "  nearAll   require EVERY entry in near (only the anvil does).",
    "  needTool  a tool that must already be owned.",
    "  maxTier   gate: the named tier must currently be BELOW this value.",
    "  armorSlot gate: an armor slot of that rank must still be upgradeable.",
    "",
    "\u26a0 Transcribed from the client's canCraft/doCraft pair, preserving behaviour",
    "exactly rather than tidying it. Two oddities are deliberate and are NOT bugs",
    "introduced here \u2014 they were already live, and silently changing them would be",
    "a balance change smuggled in under a refactor:",
    "  \u2022 'wall' gates on holding a plank but spends nothing; the plank is consumed",
    "    when the wall is actually placed. Hence requires, not cost.",
    "  \u2022 'iron_pick' has no maxTier gate, so it can be re-crafted at any tier.",
    "    Every other tier upgrade has one."
  ],
